cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use bipred, please cite the software and the method(s) used. bipred has no paper of its own yet; the references below cover the implemented methods and their direct interpretation."
title: "bipred: two-trait genetic correlation, heritability and polygenic-overlap inference from GWAS summary statistics"
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of bivariate LDpred2-style inference: bipred jointly
  fits two GWAS traits against one ancestry-matched LD reference and returns
  SNP heritabilities, genetic correlation (r_g), posterior-mean effects for
  prediction, and a MiXeR-style polygenic-overlap summary, alongside a
  cross-trait LD Score regression moment estimator. Inference uses a blocked
  Gaussian-mixture Gibbs sampler over dense or low-rank LD representations
  provided by ldpred3.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vilhjálmsson"
    given-names: "Bjarni Jóhann"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bvilhjal/bipred"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.16.dev0
keywords:
  - genetic correlation
  - polygenic overlap
  - SNP heritability
  - LDpred
  - LD Score regression
  - MiXeR
  - GWAS summary statistics
